Subject: chrome/m156:[M156][graphite] Fix PaintParamsKey comparison operator

* The PaintParamsKey operator== incorrectly memcmp on the element count of
the data, not the size in bytes of the data.

Bug: 573263908
Fixed: 578797497
Change-Id: I96119d616fcd0d44aae5940b22317a76c6c6164e
Reviewed-on: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1405816
Auto-Submit: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1c2b83b5af8f53181742af1505edd18c2418c777)
Reviewed-on: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1408119
Reviewed-by: Nathan Sanchez <nathanasanchez@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Nathan Sanchez <nathanasanchez@google.com>

diff --git a/src/gpu/graphite/PaintParamsKey.h b/src/gpu/graphite/PaintParamsKey.h
index e88443dc1d39be86d8e58b28473473d334130e32..7d5ec49833c3533bc5b75a964fc1e1f691ff26c1 100644
--- a/src/gpu/graphite/PaintParamsKey.h
+++ b/src/gpu/graphite/PaintParamsKey.h
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@ public:
 
     bool operator==(const PaintParamsKey& that) const {
         return fData.size() == that.fData.size() &&
-               !memcmp(fData.data(), that.fData.data(), fData.size());
+               !memcmp(fData.data(), that.fData.data(), fData.size_bytes());
     }
     bool operator!=(const PaintParamsKey& that) const { return !(*this == that); }
 
